.th CHESS VI 11/1/73
.sh NAME
chess \*- the game of chess
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /usr/games/chess
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Chess
is a computer program that plays class D chess.
Moves may be given either in standard (descriptive) notation
or in algebraic notation.
The symbol `+' is used to specify check;
`o-o' and `o-o-o' specify castling.
The
.it chess
program accepts the following options:
.s3
.nf
	first		play black
	resign		resign game
	save		save the game in \fIchess.out\fR
	remove		replay last set of moves
	restore		continue saved game in \fIchess.out\fR
	clock		print clock times
	score		print game history
	hint		suggest a move
	repeat		repeat last move
.fi
.s3
Each move is echoed in the appropriate notation followed by
the program's reply.
The board may be printed by typing an empty line.
.sh FILES
/usr/lib/book		opening `book'
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
The most cryptic diagnostic is `eh?' which
means that the input was syntactically incorrect.
.sh WARNING
Over-use of this program
will cause it to go away.
.sh BUGS
Pawns may be promoted only to queens.
